Feature: Old information
  The station does not hide a plane that goes quiet. The marker stays where the plane was
  last heard, and it goes dim. After a minute the marker goes away.

  Expectation: A plane that goes quiet goes stale
    Given the map has 1 other plane
    And the marker of the other plane is live
    When the other plane is silent
    And 10 seconds pass
    Then the marker of the other plane is stale

  Expectation: A quiet plane leaves the map after a minute
    Given the map has 1 other plane
    And the marker of the other plane is stale
    When 70 seconds pass
    Then the map has 0 other planes

  Expectation: A lost radio link makes every marker stale
    The station only hears the other planes through the TX15. If the link is lost, the station
    does not know where they are. It keeps the last positions, and it dims them.
    Given the map has 1 other plane
    And the marker of the other plane is live
    When the TX15 link is lost
    And 10 seconds pass
    Then the marker of the other plane is stale
